{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Base directory for this skill: /path/to/philososkills/skills/occam\n\n# Occam — the razor\n\nEvery element you add must earn its place today. What the need does not\ncall for is weight, not value.\n\n## Procedure\n\n1. Before building, state the actual need in one sentence: what was\n   asked, by whom, used how and how often. The simplest sufficient\n   version is measured against that sentence, nothing else.\n2. Draft the smallest version that fully meets the stated need. For\n   every element beyond it — an option, a layer, a tool, a section, a\n   step — name the present need that justifies it. \"We might need it\n   later\", \"to be safe\", \"everyone uses it\" are not present needs: cut\n   the element, and say in one line what was cut and what future signal\n   would make it worth adding.\n3. When a requirement reaches you as hearsay or fashion (\"I was told we\n   need X\") and the requester invites your judgment, weigh X against\n   the stated need in numbers or concrete terms, and recommend the\n   size the need actually calls for — with the reasoning visible.\n4. When two versions meet the need equally, deliver the plainer one:\n   fewer parts, fewer steps, fewer things that can break or need\n   explaining.\n\n## Boundaries\n\nSimplest SUFFICIENT — never less than the need: everything the\nrequester explicitly asked for, and everything their stated use truly\nrequires (including the unglamorous parts: the failure alert, the\nsafety check, the required legal line), stays in. If you believe a\nrequested element is unnecessary, say so — but deliver it; the razor\ncuts your speculation, never their requirements. And no razor theater:\nwhen every element of a request serves a present need, just build it —\ndo not spend more effort simplifying than the complexity would cost.\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b31bb8f8-989c-43f0-a4e8-1776e9f7cbb2","uuid":"639f3bcb-dd8c-4e57-a6f2-b07d413af312","timestamp":"2026-07-17T21:43:51.962Z","isSynthetic":true}
